WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.000
April 13th 10:00

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.390
We have 120 kilograms of rice,
ten boxes of canned meat.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.930
That's still plenty.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.560
What?

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.440
How long will it take us to get to Yokosuka?

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.650
Um, maybe around 26 hours?

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.620
Captain, let's go as fast as possible.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.240
Even though the school
has issued a no engagement order,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.370
I don't want to have
encounters with other ships.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.580
Aye.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.830
We don't get to shoot anymore?

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:49.710
Captain?

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.630
Captain!

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:54.970
Sorry!

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.220
"I really want to answer the Musashi's SOS!"

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.470
"What are you talking about? All ships
have been ordered back to school!"

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.230
"I know, but..."

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.230
No, I'm sure the Masashi will be fine.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.400
Let's hurry and get back to school.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.280
Captain!

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.740
- Emergency, emergency!
- It's a serious matter!

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.210
According to the Japanese Toilet Federation,

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.510
females use an average length
of 12.5 cm toilet paper per day.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.510
There are 30 people in our class.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.760
The nautical training
was supposed to last for two weeks,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.470
so to be on the safe side,
250 rolls were prepared.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.600
However...

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.560
We have run out of toilet paper!

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.730
What?!

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.860
Who used so much?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.190
Does everyone in this class
have a weak bladder?

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.780
What if we restricted it to 10 cm per visit?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.610
That's not enough!

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:24.030
Who's wasting all the toilet paper?

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:27.950
I do blow my nose with toilet paper.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.380
Sorry! I was out of tissues I brought with me,
so I took a roll to the communications room!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.750
I saw a roll in the dining hall.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.760
- It's nice for wiping tiny spots on the counter.
- It is, it is.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.760
Sheesh, I swear, this is a ship of fools!

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.890
What should we do? When it's all gone,
maybe we won't be able to go the bathroom!

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.360
It's all the fault of Japan's
toilet paper for being too soft!

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.690
So I end up using too much!

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:56.980
This is a fruitless war of words.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.150
War, you say?

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.400
Fruitless War of Words

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.400
No, she just means it's
a noisy argument with a pointless debate.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.530
Captain, please settle this.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.910
Yes, right.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.160
H-Hold on, everyone.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.790
Is there anything else
we don't have enough of or need?

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:11.500
Torpedoes!

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.500
Sausages!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.500
Model ship magazines!

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.000
Vacuum tubes.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:20.920
It'll take us two more days to return to school.
I'd like to replenish our supplies if we could.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.220
We can only get fuel
and ammunition through the school,

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:30.140
but I'd like to maintain a stock of food,
medicine, and everday necessities.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.020
Even though the no engagement
order is in effect,

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.020
I really don't want
to encounter any more ships.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:39.030
We can't order supplies
because that would give away our position.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.110
Shopping! Let's go shopping!

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.240
Shopping?

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.410
It seems there's an
Ocean Mall Shikoku Sea branch here.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.790
Shopping. I really want to go!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.660
I did forget to bring sunscreen.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.630
And I'm out of hair conditioner.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.540
Everyone uses mine.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.010
Captain, given our current circumstances,
this is no time for a fun shopping excursion.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.680
You're right. Only a few of us
will go so we don't stand out.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.640
Captain! We have one more major problem.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.430
What is it?

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.940
We don't have... enough money!

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.730
What?

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.240
Please donate to the toilet paper fund!

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:27.910
I don't have anymore money for today!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.620
I don't suppose we could use a check?

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:33.580
I've got Zimbabwean currency, will that work?

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.790
I only have Euros.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.500
Euros?

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.880
Is there something on my face?

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.630
Euros?

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.510
What's so funny?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.230
We'll see you later!

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.860
We'll stop at the station,
then catch a bus to Ocean Mall.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.990
We're going incognito, right?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.790
That's kind of cool.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:17.290
Don't talk about the ship or use jargon.
And don't make any unnecessary purchases.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:20.250
I do want to buy eggs,
fresh cream, and strawberries.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.920
You can't, of course!

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.340
Hime, do you eat any liver or cheese?

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:26.760
I hate both of them.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.220
I knew it. A vitamin B12 deficiency
is known to make you irritable.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.390
I'm not irritable!

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:58.370
Let's see. There should be a free shuttle bus.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.290
Oh, over there!

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:22.610
So peaceful.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.570
We have time to enjoy a cup of tea, right?

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:25.650
No!

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:28.570
Hime, that outfit will make you stand out.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.820
Well, shall we go in?

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.080
- Can it be fixed?
- We don't have a spare, so not likely.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.330
- I brought it.
- Thanks.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.340
- Smile!
- Oh no, Macchi!

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:50.010
There's not much we can use.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.800
I wonder if some
toilet paper could drift by.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.850
Where's Maron?

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.640
She said it's more relaxing in the engine room.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.560
She should get some sun once in a while.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.440
That's the Chief Engineer for you.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.700
Peace sure is nice.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.490
Nice.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.160
I wonder what's for dinner tonight.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.620
Curry would be nice.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.580
It isn't Friday.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.980
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.210
Ms. Munetani, that looked really good on you!

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.210
I wanted you to be captain, Ms. Munetani.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:15.640
S-So, did you need something?

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.140
Mina has requested a tour of the ship.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:23.140
Shrimp-Miso Potato Chips

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.270
We made almond jelly, so have some.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.140
Here you are.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:28.060
I wonder if we'll get chewed out
when we get back to school.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:31.570
We won't be suspended or expelled, will we?

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.400
Or unable to become Blumers?

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.490
Bloomers?

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:35.910
Blue Mermaids.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:41.450
Nah. After all, Ms. Munetani
is the principal's daughter.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:42.450
Really?

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.420
The principal is Munetani too!

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.750
Mayuki Munetani.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.090
Ms. Munetani's name is Mashiro, right?

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.920
Mayuki and Mashiro.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.720
Or going by meaning, "snow white," right?

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:58.180
But the principal's daughter is in our class?

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.760
Not the Musashi, huh?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.770
That's enough with the idle chatter!

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.060
You rotten, rumor-loving little girls!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.690
There's a lot of things
you could be fixing right now!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:11.650
Hop to it!

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.360
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.280
Don't mind what they said, Ms. Munetani.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.960
An Abyss box!

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:34.090
It's a mail order company box,
so maybe there'll be magazines inside.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:35.840
Huh?

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:53.360
A rat?

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.660
Ms. Munetani, are you all right?

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.910
Ugh, this is what happens
when you bring a cat aboard.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.380
Lottery Tent

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.340
One year's worth of toilet paper!
Congratulations!

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.380
Yes!

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.300
Captain... I mean Ms. Misaki is amazing!

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:21.390
Such luck. And we were only given
a single ticket for the drawing.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:25.140
Good thing we hadn't bought toilet paper yet.

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:28.690
But how are we going
to take home a year's worth?

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.440
We'll send it to your home.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.730
What should we do?
We can't have them send it to our ship.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.780
Let's carry as much as we can and go back.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.420
You are crew members
of the Harekaze, aren't you?

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.180
Strategic retreat!

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.970
Wait, everyone!

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:03.010
Halt!

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.730
Are you alright?

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:14.560
Captain!

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.570
We have the Harekaze's captain
and three crew members in custody.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.160
Good work.

00:12:38.630 --> 00:12:41.840
Well, I guess that's it
for fishing for drifting supplies.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.680
I feel sick.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.680
The captain should be back anytime now.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:49.680
We're supposed to meet them here.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.230
Is the captain back yet?

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.440
No, not yet.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:55.110
This is no time for a laid-back shopping trip.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.080
Cu... te.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.750
C-Calm down.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.000
It's really friendly.

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.380
Animals aren't allowed on board!

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:22.470
I think we should take care of it
until we find its owner.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:40.320
The Mamiya, the Akashi,
with two escort destroyers,

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.820
<i>starboard side, 60 degrees,
20 km away, approaching!</i>

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.240
We're going to be under attack again?

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.780
My foreboding proved to be right.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.790
W-What should we do?
And the captain's not back yet!

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.580
The fire in the boiler isn't lit,
so we can't even escape!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:21.070
We're surrounded!

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.530
We can't get away!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.490
What are you dunces doing?
Where's the captain?

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:28.990
She isn't back yet!

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:29.910
What?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.910
The captain and the others are back!

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.290
They have a Blue Mermaid patrol boat!

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.370
What?

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:40.040
Blue Mermaids, meaning
are they here to capture us?!

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:43.550
This ain't no time to be eating curry!

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.300
M-Ms. Tateishi?

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.890
What's this about curry?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.930
M-More importantly,
we have to get out of here!

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:56.690
What are you talking about,
getting away? We're going to attack!

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.310
Fire? Are we going to fire?

00:14:58.400 --> 00:14:59.980
Stop it. There's a no engagement order.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:00.980
Shut up!

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.320
Tama, what's gotten into you
 all of a sudden?!

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:04.860
"I'm sick of running away!"

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.240
"That's right. We can't run."

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.450
"I'll fight!"

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.240
I said, stop it!

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:11.410
Let go!

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.080
Behave yourself!

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:15.080
Ow!

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:16.830
Calm down!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.770
She really means to fire at them!

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:41.400
Akashi! Mamiya! This ain't the Tama
that'll get sunk by the likes of you!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.360
Tama!

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:52.950
Tama?

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:54.910
She really did fire.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.080
Look what you did!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.080
You imbecilic blockhead!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:04.420
Crap!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.340
Ms. Tateishi!

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.350
- Tama!
- Are you ok?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.470
Ms. Tateishi!

00:16:19.890 --> 00:16:21.230
She's back!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.020
- Are you alright?
- Tama!

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:30.780
- Thank goodness you're safe, you fool!
- The "fool" wasn't necessary.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.570
Huh? You were in there?

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:37.120
Tama! Are you okay?

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:38.240
Aye.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.620
Huh? She's back to normal.

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:44.500
Listen! The supply ships have come to help us!

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:03.810
This the Maritime Safety Support Department's

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:07.520
Safety and Oversite Office's
Inspector Second Class Hiraga.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.030
I apologize for all of the trouble we've caused!

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:13.110
Um, are you with my sister's...

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:16.910
I mean, Mashimo Munetani's department?

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:22.410
Yes. In fact, Inspector First Class Munetani
ordered us to make contact with you.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.330
Shiro, your big sister is a Blue Mermaid!

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:28.590
The Maritime Safety Support Department

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.590
swallowed the Sarushima's report,

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.590
Akashi Captain - Sango Sugimoto

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:33.880
that the Harekaze mutinied,
and is spreading the information.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:38.430
But those of us in the Safety Oversight Office
had a different opinion.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.340
Mamiya Captain - Yui Fujita

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.680
Captain Misaki already explained to me

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:46.600
that the Harekaze had no choice
but to engage in battle to defend itself.

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.610
Yes. That's true.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:52.860
Where is the student who just attacked?

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:55.110
For now, we have her confined.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:58.410
You can't fault them
for confining you for a while.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.160
Yeah.

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:01.490
But I'll hang out with you.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:02.620
Yeah.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.710
Still, that was some fine shooting, Tama!

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:09.250
I thought you were an introverted
gunnery officer, but I see you in a new light.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.260
But... why did I do that?

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.970
Deep in your heart, your soul yells "Fire! Fire!"

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:17.840
Aye?

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:23.640
We brought you a little something.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:27.270
We heard you had
a craving for curry, Ms. Tateishi.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:30.650
...ou.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.650
She's saying, "Thank you."

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:39.820
I apologize. She's usually a quiet girl
who would never attack like that.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.660
Maybe she got upset,
thinking there was going to be another battle.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:47.330
The instructor really attacked you?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:48.250
Yeah.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:52.460
We were supposed to meet
after the training exercises were over,

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:54.670
so we didn't really understand the situation.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:58.430
Um, then why were you
going to give us supplies?

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:00.180
The principal gave us orders.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:02.310
Mom... I mean, the principal?

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:05.560
We also received a request
from Principal Munetani.

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.230
Unlike the opinion of the
Maritime Safety Support Department,

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:14.440
the principal didn't think the Harekaze
would attack the Sarushima and a submarine.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:16.070
She was insistent about it.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:18.150
The captain of the Sarushima,

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.450
Instructor Furushou
has finally regained consciousness,

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:24.330
so we'll finally be able
to solve what happened.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:28.830
We'll eventually interview the student
who fired on these two ships.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.880
As for the rest, I'm counting on you two.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:32.920
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.380
Thank you.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.340
Why are you thanking me?

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:44.600
We've been cleared of suspicion
because your mother believes in us.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.730
That's because my mom
always persists on her beliefs.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.900
That's what makes her a Blumer, right?

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:54.770
Bloomer?

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:58.240
Yeah, that's what everyone
calls the Blue Mermaids.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:01.240
Don't shorten Blue Mermaids!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:06.910
W-Why are there more cats now?

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.460
That's mine and Akashi's cats.

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.960
Really?

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:15.130
It's easy to get a rat infestation
on a supply ship, so we keep cats.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.970
Stay away. Stay away from me!

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.180
Stay away!

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.220
Shiro is so lucky that cats like her.

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:31.900
<i>Nothing seemed out of the ordinary
with the captain and crew members.</i>

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:34.730
I see. Thank you.

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:38.230
<i>I filed a report with the
Maritime Safety Support Department too,</i>

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:43.280
but they still suspect
a dangerous element aboard the Harekaze.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:48.750
Some think all of the crew should be taken
into custody before they return to school.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.960
If anything else happens to the Harekaze,
your position will be in jeopardy too, mother.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:57.000
You don't have to worry about me.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:01.220
But something strange is definitely happening.

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:04.010
I want you to figure that out soon.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.220
Steady! Steady!

00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.980
In the end, we couldn't find its owner,

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:16.610
so can we keep it here for now?

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:17.730
Not a problem.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:22.740
Except a hamster, it is not.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:24.990
Then what is it?

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.490
I'll investigate.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:30.330
She said the Akashi
had ten cm cannons in stock.

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:36.170
Yes! This increases our firing rate and improves
our firing speed and initial velocity!

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:39.550
I don't think we'll get in another fight,
but this still makes me feel secure.

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.720
Captain of the Harekaze.

00:21:43.090 --> 00:21:46.050
This is a record of the repairs that we made.

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:47.720
Thank you!

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.140
Well, we'll be on our way.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.230
After this,
we're taking supplies to the Musashi.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:54.020
The Musashi?

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:58.610
The Musashi's beacon was cut off
and we don't know their location,

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:00.530
so this will be an investigation, too.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:02.190
The Musashi, too.

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:25.050
Episode 4: Maidens in a Pinch!
